\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For Schwartz functions f1,f2,f3 on R, let $T(f1,f2,f3)(x)=pv$ integral f1(x+t)f2(x+2t)f3(x+3t) dt/t. Is $||T(f1,f2,f3)||_L1$ $<=$ C $product_j$ $||fj||_L3$ for one finite absolute C?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For Schwartz functions f1,f2,f3 on R, let $T(f1,f2,f3)(x)=pv$ integral f1(x+t)f2(x+2t)f3(x+3t) dt/t. Is $||T(f1,f2,f3)||_L1$ $<=$ C $product_j$ $||fj||_L3$ for one finite absolute C?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://terrytao.wordpress.com/2007/05/10/open-question-boundedness-of-the-trilinear-hilbert-transform/}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/An-L3-bound-for-the-trilinear-Hilbert-transform-October-5-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

